        }
      ],
      "message": "util: make STATIC_ASSERT usable at file scope\n\nReplace the switch-based STATIC_ASSERT, which is a statement and thus\nonly usable inside functions, with a declaration-like macro. It uses\n_Static_assert in C11 mode and, as an extension, with GCC >= 4.6 and\nClang in pre-C11 modes. Other compilers fall back to declaring an\nextern array whose size is negative if the assertion fails.\n\nSince STATIC_ASSERT now expands to a declaration, move its use in\nsecp256k1_ge_impl_to_bytes before VERIFY_CHECK to avoid mixing\ndeclarations and code, which C89 forbids.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Tim Ruffing",
        "email": "me@real-or-random.org",
        "date": "2026-10-01T15:40:27Z"
      },
